# Core Architecture & Development Patterns ✅

## Overview

Juno is a production-ready Tauri v2 desktop application implementing a hierarchical AI Computer Use agent system with advanced voice integration and cloud connectivity. This rule documents the core architectural patterns and development guidelines.

## Project Structure

### Key Directories
- **[src-tauri/](mdc:src-tauri)** - Rust backend with agent system and tools
- **[src/](mdc:src)** - React/TypeScript frontend with floating UI
- **[tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription)** - Voice processing plugin
- **[src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level)** - OS-level MCP server

### Core Architecture Files
- **[src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs)** - Tauri app initialization and command registration
- **[src-tauri/src/state.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/state.rs)** - Centralized application state management
- **[src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs)** - Main orchestrator agent entry point
- **[ARCHITECTURE.md](mdc:ARCHITECTURE.md)** - Detailed architectural documentation

## Hierarchical Agent System ⭐

### Agent Architecture Pattern
```
Orchestrator Agent (Persistent Memory + Personality)
    ↓ delegates to
Specialist Agents (Fresh Memory + Domain Expertise)
    ↓ uses
Shared Tool Providers (Lazy Initialization + Thread Safety)
```

### Implementation Pattern
```rust
// Orchestrator - Persistent conversation memory
let memory_manager = app_state.get_memory_manager().await;

// Specialists - Fresh memory for task isolation
let memory_manager = SimpleMemoryManager::new();

// Shared resources - Arc-based thread safety
pub browser_controller: Arc<TokioMutex<Option<BrowserController>>>,
```

### Agent Roles
- **Orchestrator** ([anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs)): Task analysis, delegation, conversation continuity
- **Browser Agent** ([agents/browser_agent.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agents/browser_agent.rs)): Web automation and content extraction
- **Desktop Agent** ([agents/desktop_agent.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agents/desktop_agent.rs)): Native app interaction and UI automation
- **File Agent** ([agents/file_agent.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agents/file_agent.rs)): Code editing and file system operations

## State Management Patterns

### AppState Structure
Located in [src-tauri/src/state.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/state.rs), follows consistent patterns:

```rust
pub struct AppState {
    // Memory management - orchestrator level
    memory_manager: Arc<TokioMutex<SimpleMemoryManager>>,

    // Shared resources - lazy initialization
    browser_controller: Arc<TokioMutex<Option<BrowserController>>>,

    // Configuration state
    agent_mode: Arc<TokioMutex<AgentMode>>,

    // Cloud connectivity
    cloud_client: Arc<TokioMutex<Option<CloudClient>>>,
    cloud_enabled: Arc<Mutex<bool>>,

    // Thread safety pattern: Arc<TokioMutex<T>> for async, Arc<Mutex<T>> for sync
}
```

### State Access Pattern
```rust
// Async access to shared state
let memory_guard = app_state.memory_manager.lock().await;

// Clone Arc for function parameters
let memory_manager = Arc::clone(&app_state.memory_manager);

// Safe state modification
app_state.set_agent_mode(new_mode).await;
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### AgentError System
Centralized error handling via [src-tauri/src/agent/error.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/error.rs):

```rust
// Never use std::process::exit() - use AgentError instead
return Err(AgentError::ToolExecution(format!("Tool failed: {}", error)));

// Proper error propagation
pub async fn some_function() -> Result<Value, AgentError> {
    // Implementation
}
```

### Error Categories
- **ToolExecution**: Tool-specific failures with context
- **ValidationError**: Input validation failures
- **NetworkError**: Connection and communication issues
- **SecurityError**: Permission and authorization failures

## Tool System Patterns

### Tool Definition Pattern
```rust
// Standard tool registration in ToolProvider
ToolDefinition {
    name: "descriptive_tool_name".to_string(),
    description: "Clear description for AI model understanding".to_string(),
    input_schema: serde_json::to_value(InputSchema).unwrap(),
}
```

### Tool Categories
- **[commands/](mdc:src-tauri/src/commands)** - Direct system interaction (mouse, keyboard, screen)
- **[agent/tools/](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools)** - Higher-level agent tools (browser, timer, MCP)
- **[cloud/](mdc:src-tauri/src/cloud)** - Cloud connectivity and remote execution

### Tool Implementation Pattern
```rust
// Async tool with proper error handling
pub async fn tool_function(
    app_handle: AppHandle,
    parameter: String,
) -> Result<ToolResult, AgentError> {
    let app_state = app_handle.state::<AppState>();

    // Implementation with error propagation
    match operation().await {
        Ok(result) => Ok(ToolResult::success(result)),
        Err(e) => Err(AgentError::ToolExecution(format!("Failed: {}", e))),
    }
}
```

